{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1143316-void-engineers-and-spy-game","id":1143316,"title":"Void Engineers and Spy Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-23T14:18:41-07:00","id":1143316,"title":"Void Engineers and Spy Game","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....The Fleet Intelligence Service (predictably referred to as \u201cSpooks\u201d) is the Fleet\u2019s central analysis platform for information coming in from all our operational fronts. Its members are found in their primary offices on Station Yemaja and Copernicus Station.<br /> Roughly 10% of its personnel do field analysis in co-ops and Constructs throughout the Universe.<br /> In the field, they wear black issue uniforms with no decoration outside of rank and name. These operatives have access to every aspect and section of their assigned environments, and don\u2019t talk about their missions unless absolutely necessary. This breeds an equal measure of resentment and curiosity in the Engineers they work with. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...With the destruction of the Sentinel network around the Near Horizon and the construction of the ITAG, the Intelligence Directorate (ID) now focuses its energies on monitoring the Deep and Near Universe. It shares that intelligence with the rest of the Convention, frequently clashing with R&amp;E\u2019s FIS. </div> </div> </div>These paragraphs caught my attention. FIS appears to be an extremely fascinating concept...and utterly unexpected element.<br /> <br /> Sadly, above citations were only information available to me regarding them.<br /> <br /> So what are they? What is their mission? And what <i>90%</i> of their personnel are doing in the shadow, at the back of their comrades? Is it an autonomous military and/or espionage organization in VE, essentially a micro-Convention, completed with its own ships, equipment, installations, command chain and structure? Is there connection between them and NWO, especially the Operatives?<br /> <br /> Have you any idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 09-23-2017, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T14:50:57-07:00","id":1143330,"title":"","content":"Something between a very scary hands on version of SIGINT, Babylon 5 Psi Corps and the Political Officers of the old Soviet Union?<br /> <br /> If you want it to be it's own Methodology with a parallel infrastructure, that sounds fine. I think VE's are a bit more thin on the ground (across the sky) than that (at least for my games), since they don't just cover Conventional Space (though that's always been their focus to me), but also serving as the &quot;Sentinels on the Gauntlet&quot; against all the other version of the Umbra, the hunters of EDEs that escape on the Earth and the explorers of the unexplored regions of Earth as well. So I would have them be something of a Methodology that doesn't have many installations of its own, but operates as ombudsmen that tag along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","na